{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers","id":29692,"title":"Apotheosis and Guild Status (probably some spoilers)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-13T20:45:01-08:00","id":29692,"title":"Apotheosis and Guild Status (probably some spoilers)","content":"Okay, so taking as a given that a lot of the text on apotheosis, even in the storyteller section, is extremely vague (if &quot;off the supernatural radar&quot; isn't a phrase that is wildly up for interpretation, I don't know what is)...<br /> <br /> It seems to me, from reading Guildhalls, that Guild Status is set up so that it doesn't just....disappear, if you stop showing up to meetings or if everyone forgets your name. It has to be actively stripped from you in order to be lost. So does that mean that you keep it after apotheosis? I mean, obviously you won't be able to use it most of the time: if you come out of the woodwork and start using your Guild Status 5 to boss around the Journeymen, they're going to cry foul pretty quickly. And likewise, you probably can't gain <i>more</i>. But the mystical aspect of the status (and the guild affinities that come with it) should stay with you assuming no one remembers you long enough to track you down, hold you still, and perform an Obloquy, right?<br /> <br /> Just looking for a sanity check here, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T22:17:18-08:00","id":29742,"title":"","content":"It's a good question that really doesn't have an answer.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I mean you're a free mummy now, no longer bound to the judges will or the call of the ancient relics. You've got a brand new unlife ahead of you without needing to return to sleep. But that also brings a lot of trouble. It would be difficult to give up the guild, an organization and congregation you've been a part of for literally thousands of years. It would be even harder to give up on your meret, the mummies you call allies. And remember, Apotheosis is a myth. The stuff of legends. Who's going to believe you? Some may even get mad at you for reminding them of something they cannot possess.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I bet it would be hard for a mummy to give up their guild. It's basically their entire way of life since before time began. But on the other hand it would be dangerous or foolish to reveal yourself as an apotheosis mummy. Though someone's going to notice that you've got less power and you don't need to return to your rest, and your form doesn't change. An apotheosis brings freedom but it also bars you out of a world you've been a part of for all you're unlife. What's a mummy to do?<br /> <br /> In terms of the game, I assume you keep it until you rescind your status for someone else, or the other mummies just forget about you.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T05:03:50-08:00","id":29839,"title":"","content":"Since the thread title is marked with a spoiler warning I don't think you need to put spoilers in your post, RisTigger, though I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Interesting question, OP. The Guild structure the Arisen exist in was sort of 're-constructed' by them, when they arose in the first Sothic turn (judging by the Sothic cycle page in the core book, and other mentions of Guilds being that they're, well, re-constructed from what they remembered of their mortal roles in the Empire), It's become such a powerful identity to them that <i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i> goes out and says this Y-splat is more integral to the Arisen than other Y-splats are to other splats, and that the Guild magic which infuses a Mummy is second only to the Rite of Return itself.<br /> <br /> So it's hard to imagine that something so ingrained into the Arisen would be shed upon Apotheosis, which doesn't even completely strip them of the Rite. Apotheosis isn't like the New Dawn in Promethean. It's not about necessarily becoming human (although you do, in a sense, because it's about reclaiming Memory) but rather unbinding yourself from the chains of Duat. Since it doesn't strip away the Rite, and therefore your affinities, utterances, and Pillars, I can't imagine it stripping away belonging to a Guild.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, no Guild wants anything to do with an Arisen who has achieved Apotheosis. Perhaps I might rule it like the Guild effectively removes your Status, but you get to keep your Guild affinities? The Guild doesn't recognize you, even though the Rite itself does...or something.<br /> <br /> This might be what's so unsettling about the Deceived, actually! The teasers we know of them thus far, between hints in <i>Guildhalls</i> and things CAS has posted here lately, seem to imply they know something about Apotheosis. I don't think they've achieved it, but they have some sort of connection with it and they <i>are</i> a Guild after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T07:41:14-08:00","id":29901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>reseru:</b><br /> Perhaps I might rule it like the Guild effectively removes your Status, but you get to keep your Guild affinities? </div> </div> </div>That seems logical; in a way, Guild is ingrained into the mummy to the point of being a selectable bio-splat rather than a social one. I'd suggest adding that the process of changing Guild, which is hard at the best of times, is closed to you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T15:03:34-08:00","id":30110,"title":"","content":"Guildhalls actually has rules for apotheosis mummys losing or trying to retain their guild affinities. It's on pg. 88, last paragraph of Loss. Also &quot;Guild Affinities cannot be stolen and misused by apostates&quot;. For Utterances, you still retain the ones you learned even after apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T17:27:30-08:00","id":30162,"title":"","content":"I assumed &quot;apostate&quot; in that context meant &quot;mummies who switched guilds&quot;. There's nothing to obviously indicate that they're referring to apotheosis there (despite looking similar and having the same prefix, 'apostate' and 'apotheosis' aren't tightly semantically linked. The former means 'someone who forsook their creed', the latter refers to becoming a god). Also, they established the fact that apostates couldn't use those affinities <i>because</i> the affinities were mystically linked to guild status, all of which is presumably stripped during the same ceremony in which you switch guilds. Which brings us back to the question of whether ascended mummies get to keep their status assuming no one is around to take it away from them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 12-14-2013, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T17:41:35-08:00","id":30166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers?p=29839#post29839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be what's so unsettling about the Deceived, actually! The teasers we know of them thus far, between hints in <i>Guildhalls</i> and things CAS has posted here lately, seem to imply they know something about Apotheosis. I don't think they've achieved it, but they have some sort of connection with it and they <i>are</i> a Guild after all</div> </div> </div> </div>This is totally off-topic, and also complete speculation on my part, but I think we may discover that achieving apotheosis is an irrelevant concept for the Deceived. They very obviously <i>already aren't</i> beholden to the judges, since the judges tried to kill them off entirely and they noticeably didn't die. What's unclear from what little we've heard about them is whether they were killed off before or after the Rite was performed on them. If after, then it seems they've achieved apotheosis somehow, possibly as part of whatever allowed them to survive their destruction, as they certainly don't seem to be serving the judges now. If before, then they seem to have found some way to perform some version of the rite <i>on themselves</i>, thus making apotheosis unnecessary. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T21:43:52-08:00","id":30263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers?p=30166#post30166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is totally off-topic, and also complete speculation on my part, but I think we may discover that achieving apotheosis is an irrelevant concept for the Deceived. They very obviously <i>already aren't</i> beholden to the judges, since the judges tried to kill them off entirely and they noticeably didn't die. What's unclear from what little we've heard about them is whether they were killed off before or after the Rite was performed on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure they don't serve the Judges? Even the Deathless that do serve the Judges often fight amongst each other, so what's to preclude the Deceived?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GABBY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If after, then it seems they've achieved apotheosis somehow, possibly as part of whatever allowed them to survive their destruction, as they certainly don't seem to be serving the judges now. If before, then <i>they seem to have found some way to perform some version of the rite </i><i>on themselves</i>, thus making apotheosis unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T23:21:38-08:00","id":30303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers?p=30162#post30162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed &quot;apostate&quot; in that context meant &quot;mummies who switched guilds&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's just a flaw in the design right there, obviously! I am not wrong! Just joking of course, thanks for clarifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers?p=30162#post30162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If after, then it seems they've achieved apotheosis somehow, possibly as part of whatever allowed them to survive their destruction, as they certainly don't seem to be serving the judges now. If before, then they seem to have found some way to perform some version of the rite <i>on themselves</i>, thus making apotheosis unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, even the Shuankshen serve a judge. The Deceived must have someone they serve, if it's not the judges (they were a guild remember).<br /> <br /> And do we know they have achieves apotheosis? We know they have a connection with it, but have all of them achieved it? I have my doubts they have for some reason. I am SOOOO looking forward to the Book of the Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T01:17:31-08:00","id":30328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers?p=30263#post30263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you figure they don't serve the Judges? Even the Deathless that do serve the Judges often fight amongst each other, so what's to preclude the Deceived?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going from the assumption that the judges wanted them dead (in the permanent way) and they somehow found a way to continue to be alive. That doesn't sound like a group of people who are still being sponsored by the judges. Their continued existence is presumably against the judges' orders. We also know that they aren't subject to the same memory degradation, which was built into the Arisen <i>by the judges</i> to keep their servants from getting uppity. Both of those point to a group of people who are off the reservation, if they were ever on it. <br /> <br /> The Shuankhsen are a different issue, because the shuankhsen serve an entity (Ammut) that the judges cannot overpower. The Shuankhsen are sponsored by <i>someone</i>, and we haven't yet met any entity that would do the same for the deceived. (Except maybe Anpu or Sutekh? They seem like shifty rebellious sorts)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T10:22:01-08:00","id":30476,"title":"","content":"The Guildhalls book draws a connection between the Deceived and Apotheosis in more than one occasion. If the Deceived have attained Apotheosis, then it's likely that they have noone to serve other than their own interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T11:58:00-08:00","id":30513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers?p=30328#post30328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going from the assumption that the judges wanted them dead (in the permanent way) and they somehow found a way to continue to be alive. That doesn't sound like a group of people who are still being sponsored by the judges. Their continued existence is presumably against the judges' orders. We also know that they aren't subject to the same memory degradation, which was built into the Arisen <i>by the judges</i> to keep their servants from getting uppity. Both of those point to a group of people who are off the reservation, if they were ever on it.<br /> <br /> The Shuankhsen are a different issue, because the shuankhsen serve an entity (Ammut) that the judges cannot overpower. The Shuankhsen are sponsored by <i>someone</i>, and we haven't yet met any entity that would do the same for the deceived. (Except maybe Anpu or Sutekh? They seem like shifty rebellious sorts)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I guess I'm taking the exact opposite perspective haha<br /> <br /> To me, the Judges are very hands-off and distant in terms of Morally Ambiguous Otherwordly Overlords, compared to other splats. The God-machine works in mysterious ways but its motives and methods are confounding and seemingly nonsensical, and its angelic servants are mindless automatons (well, until they Fall); the Judges have a clearer goal - collect vessels imbued with Sekhem - and its agents are surprisingly individualistic (the Rite didn't intend for the Arisen to have Memory). The Exarchs and their Seer agents are a bit more interactive with the world, with understandable goals. The only way the Judges really interact with our world is their whipping of the Arisen, but even then they themselves are never seen. The only way the Arisen know if they've displeased the Judges are when they make an unscheduled Descent roll. They're very distant, ruling in a distant world and only revealing themselves when the Mummies made their Decree.<br /> <br /> So what that all means, to me, is that I don't think the Judges really cared about the Deceived, because they're distant and largely uncaring about Arisen concerns. The Mummies of the Lost Guild <i>are technically Deathless</i>, unlike the Shuankhsen, so they were presumably all made by the Rite of Return and bound to the Judges. Since the Arisen are so autonomous, though, I think that the other Guilds didn't like what the Deceived were up to and put a stop to it themselves. I haven't read anywhere that the Judges themselves had beef with the Sixth Guild; any mention of the Sixth Guild thus far makes a point to say that they're out for revenge against the Arisen, not the Judges. It's a technical difference, and I could be very, very wrong once Book of the Deceived is released.<br /> <br /> The only thing besides vessels the Judges care about, I think, are the Shuankhsen. They issued a standing order to return any and all Bane relics to Duat immediately because of their danger. The Devourer seems to be the only enemy that the Judges care to combat. Whereas the Deceived are out for revenge against the Arisen, the Shuankhsen hate them because they serve the Judges. The Arisen think they're near gods, but its Shuankhsen who have Morality instead of Memory. If anyone knows the capital-T Truth then its the Shuankhsen, in a way. Nothing yet says if the Deceived have Memory or not, but considering that they're Deathless rather than Lifeless I would be willing to bet they do.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if I come off as rude. If you have certain assumptions or conclusions I'm just curious from where you got them. I know it's all just speculation, but if there's something I missed somewhere then I'm very interested in reading the bit! You know?<br /> <br /> So all I'm saying is that I think the Judges do go out of their way to fight the Shuankhsen, since trafficking with them forces a Descent roll and fighting them earns you a Descent reset. Clearly the Deceived have a connection to Apotheosis which means they don't like serving the Judges, although they did, as Deathless and not Lifeless, make a Decree to a Judge at one point (I assume), I don't think the Judges get their hate-on for the Sixth Guild. I think the rivalry is Arisen vs Deceived, rather than Judges as Deceived, although the nature of both Deathless entities innately calls in to question Mummy-Judge relationships","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":".  added final two paragraphs 12-15-2013, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T13:52:08-08:00","id":30566,"title":"","content":"The story at the beginning of book two of the mummy book (the storyteller section) makes it pretty clear it wasn't the other mummies who screwed over the sixth guild. They got screwed <i>during</i> the rite, not afterward, and were never supposed to arise as mummies at all. Which tends to imply it was the Shan'iatu who did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T17:04:04-08:00","id":31329,"title":"","content":"i don't remember where the information about the Lost Guild all having been of the Ren decree, but.. thatd mean they all serve Sutek. Sutek is mentioned as having a rivalry with Azar (who may or may not have been Pharaoh). this could be played out in the deceived, as sutek's serpents try to overthrow azar, his judges, and their arisen legion. anpu might even help him, as he lost power when azar ascended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T04:51:40-08:00","id":31585,"title":"","content":"Yeah so reading that bit of the book closer definitely makes me see where you're coming from. It seems that the Nameless Empire isn't nameless because it &quot;didn't need a name, since it was the first&quot; but rather because the Shan'iatu cosmically ret-conned it out of existence, or at least made people forget about it. Its true name was offered in sacrifice for power, thus it became Nameless. Actually, perhaps that helped it become eternal in a way.<br /> <br /> So the Sixth Guild, as masters of true names, probably had some beef with that idea. The Shan'iatu didn't care, and the Guild got screwed. That still doesn't sound like the Judges hate the Deceived. The opposite is probably true, considering their relationship with Apotheosis. And that conclusion only fits the bill if you think the Shan'iatu and Judges are separate entities (which I do).<br /> <br /> And doesn't it say that Sutek helped Azar to the throne? That's what the Amulet of Two Fingers is all about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T13:48:33-08:00","id":31881,"title":"","content":"Indeed, but elsewhere (i can't remember where) there is a reference that the infamous rivalry of Set and Osiris is based on a real tension between Sutek and Azar. As these are Old Gods (im fairly sure Sutek is as close to cthulhu as we can get), im not suprised by contradictions. Esit, for example, is refered to as Re's wife, but also in other's as Azar's wife. Im considering the old gods as vastly removed from humanity (even the relatively sociable Anpu), and thus helping azar while also trying to destroy him doesn't shock me, nor would Esit being the Cosmic Bride to more than one diety. It would be helpful if the storytellers sections actually gave storytellers a bit more to work with, regarding the Judges and Old Gods, not to mention the specifics of the Rite of Return. I suppose theyre leaving STs in the dark until the Sothic Book (as we can use irem as a setting in that book, im assuming itll include thehuge spoilers about iremite faith and society).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T18:03:30-08:00","id":34199,"title":"","content":"So what everyone is saying is that, if an Arisen is outed as went through Apotheosis, then he/she is then shunned from the Guilds. If that's so, then wouldn't the longing of the guild structure force those who went through Apotheosis to then band together and create NEW guilds? If so, then it would be cool if some Apotheotic made a guild that is online (the cultists and the mummy discuss stuff of the Internet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T23:13:25-08:00","id":34323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/29692-apotheosis-and-guild-status-probably-some-spoilers?p=34199#post34199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what everyone is saying is that, if an Arisen is outed as went through Apotheosis, then he/she is then shunned from the Guilds. If that's so, then wouldn't the longing of the guild structure force those who went through Apotheosis to then band together and create NEW guilds? If so, then it would be cool if some Apotheotic made a guild that is online (the cultists and the mummy discuss stuff of the Internet).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the Lost Guild? Yeah I'm not sure many Apotheosis mummies are itching to join them any time soon (if they can that is...oh another question, can mummies join the Deceived?).<br /> <br /> Also guildhalls addresses your question on page 89. Is does say that Apotheosis could create a new guild...but it's not likely due to the nature of the guilds and mummies themselves. The amount of Apotheosis mummies is probably very minimal and the chances of them trying to band together to form a new guild and hammer out rules and structure is...daunting to say the least. As the book says, not impossible but good luck with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T00:45:07-08:00","id":34344,"title":"","content":"Considering that losing Guild status is based on the social order of the Guilds, I don't think the Arisen would lose the status unless hie/her Guild found out that they've archived Apothoesis.<br /> <br /> Since that idea hasn't shown up in this thread yet, I thought I would share it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}